course: dictionary
lesson: 5400
title: Kopje: a little rocky hill
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A kopje is a small hill, usually rocky, that stands alone on flat, open land. Look at the clues. «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes» tells you the kopjes are rocky, and that lions rest on them.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes, which give them shade, a lookout and safe dens for cubs.» Now read it as "lions rest on small rocky hills, which give them shade, a lookout and safe dens for cubs." It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: The clues in the sentence also show why a kopje is useful. Shade, a lookout and safe dens all come from its rocks and height. The word itself comes from Afrikaans and Dutch and means "little head", which fits a small hill that stands up on its own.
fact: A kopje is a small hill, usually rocky, that stands alone on flat, open land called the veld.
fact: «Kopje» comes from Afrikaans and Dutch, and means «little head».
fact: The plural of «kopje» is «kopjes».
fact: In geography lessons, kopjes are rocky hills on the grasslands of southern Africa, where animals such as lions rest.
fact: In history lessons about the Boer War, soldiers fought around kopjes.
exercise: «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes, which give them shade, a lookout and safe dens for cubs.» What is a kopje? | A deep river running through a forest | A flat, empty field with no rocks | A big city with tall buildings | *A small, usually rocky hill standing alone on flat open land
exercise: «Kopje» comes from Afrikaans and Dutch. What does it mean in English? | *Little head | Lion's den | Big rock | Open plain
exercise: «Real Serengeti lions rest on rocky islands called kopjes, which give shade, a lookout and safe dens, and the film makers went to East Africa to study them.» Which clue tells you kopjes are useful to lions? | The film makers went to East Africa | They are made of soft sand | They are always under water | *They give shade, a lookout and safe dens
test: In geography lessons, where do kopjes stand? | In dense rainforests | *On flat, open grassland | Under the sea | Inside tall cities
test: In history lessons, soldiers fought around kopjes. What does this suggest a kopje was good for? | A spot where it always snows | *A high, rocky place to fight from | A place to grow bananas | A place to build a swimming pool
exam: A child reads «The kopje rose alone from the flat veld.» What does kopje mean here? | A type of tall grass | A river that floods in spring | A straight, flat road | *A small, rocky hill on open land
